# Local development (npm run dev) / local Compose / kind — the browser talks to each backend
# directly on its published host port. These are also the Dockerfile's build ARG defaults, so a
# plain `docker build` with no --build-arg overrides produces the same thing.
VITE_ORDER_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8081
VITE_INVENTORY_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8082
VITE_PAYMENT_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8083
VITE_FULFILLMENT_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8084
VITE_SCENARIO_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8085

# Production build (deployed behind a single ingress — see
# docs/agent-reports/sprint-2/deployment-code-changes-briefing.md's W1/W2): pass these as relative,
# same-origin prefixes instead, e.g. via `docker build --build-arg VITE_ORDER_SERVICE_URL=/svc/order
# ...` (apiFetch and EventSource in src/api/client.ts concatenate baseUrl + path unchanged):
#
# VITE_ORDER_SERVICE_URL=/svc/order
# VITE_INVENTORY_SERVICE_URL=/svc/inventory
# VITE_PAYMENT_SERVICE_URL=/svc/payment
# VITE_FULFILLMENT_SERVICE_URL=/svc/fulfillment
# VITE_SCENARIO_SERVICE_URL=/svc/scenario
